idate_beta). It does NOT include vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha. Indeed goal does not require shift_candidate_alpha to retain its vehicle allocation; it only requires vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha and shift_candidate_beta. So we can deallocate vehicle_unit_gamma from shift_candidate_alpha by dispatching it (which will make vehicle available). After dispatch, shift_candidate_alpha will be dispatched, and vehicle_unit_gamma becomes available. Then we can allocate vehicle_unit_gamma to shift_candidate_beta later. However goal also requires vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma, and after dispatch shift_candidate_beta we need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (goal). So we will allocate, then later dispatch shift_candidate_beta to release.

